    "evidence_text": "In addition, numerous aggregates of myosin heavy chain accumulate in the sqh null cells.\n\nThe Hippo signaling pathway restricts the oncogenic potential of an intestinal regeneration program.\n\nWe find that regenerating crypts express elevated Yes-associated protein (YAP) levels.\n\nA genetic screen identifies an LKB1\u2013MARK signalling axis controlling the Hippo\u2013YAP pathway\n\nOur data also indicate that YAP is functionally important for the tumour suppressive effects of LKB1.\n\nRole of inscuteable in orienting asymmetric cell divisions in Drosophila\n\nWhat makes the two Dicers specific for their biological substrates?\n\nMechanosignaling through YAP and TAZ drives fibroblast activation and fibrosis.\n\nHowever, the molecular mechanisms underlying this process remain poorly understood.\n\nTEAD mediates YAP-dependent gene induction and growth control.\n\nRecent studies have established that YAP is phosphorylated and inhibited by the Hippo tumor suppressor pathway.\n\nCTGF is identified as a direct YAP target gene important for cell growth.\n\nA conserved phosphatase cascade that regulates nuclear membrane biogenesis.\n\nHowever, KRAS has thus far not been a viable therapeutic target.",
